---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { brand, clients, cta } from '../brand.config';
import { absolute, ORG_ID } from '../lib/seo';
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';

const description =
  'Option One is retained to design, build and integrate difficult undertakings, and to record them properly. A global operations consultancy based in London, United Kingdom.';

const serviceSchema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'Design',
    serviceType: 'System architecture, operating model and structural design',
    provider: { '@id': ORG_ID },
    areaServed: { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Worldwide' },
    url: absolute('/services/design'),
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'Build',
    serviceType: 'Operational build, systems, procedure and automation',
    provider: { '@id': ORG_ID },
    areaServed: { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Worldwide' },
    url: absolute('/services/build'),
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'Integrate',
    serviceType: 'Operational integration, training and handover',
    provider: { '@id': ORG_ID },
    areaServed: { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Worldwide' },
    url: absolute('/services/integrate'),
  },
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'Communicate',
    serviceType: 'Film, sound and written record for projects and investors',
    provider: { '@id': ORG_ID },
    areaServed: { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Worldwide' },
    url: absolute('/services/communicate'),
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  heroHeader={true}
  title="Global Operational Resilience and Delivery"
  description={description}
  schema={serviceSchema}>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-img"></div>
    <svg class="graticule" viewBox="0 0 1200 800" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" aria-hidden="true">
      <g fill="none" stroke="#7FB2C6" stroke-width="1">
        <path d="M0,160 Q600,90 1200,160" /><path d="M0,320 Q600,260 1200,320" />
        <path d="M0,480 Q600,430 1200,480" /><path d="M0,640 Q600,600 1200,640" />
        <path d="M200,0 Q150,400 200,800" /><path d="M480,0 Q450,400 480,800" />
        <path d="M720,0 Q750,400 720,800" /><path d="M1000,0 Q1050,400 1000,800" />
      </g>
    </svg>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow mono"><span class="rule"></span>{brand.disciplines}<span class="rule"></span></p>
      <h1>Difficult things, built correctly.</h1>
      <p class="lede">{brand.tagline}</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={withBase('/services')}>What we do</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={withBase(cta.href)}>{cta.label}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap sect">
      <p class="sec-mark mono">The premise</p>
      <div class="sect-body">
      <h2 class="band-title reveal">Operational risk has changed.</h2>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>For thirty years operational risk was an execution problem. Supply arrived,
        energy cleared, approvals followed, and capability could be bought at the point
        it was needed. Delivery was a question of management.</p>
        <p>That has changed. Supply, energy, minerals, labour, regulation and capital are
        now set as much by borders and politics as by the market, and the effect does not
        arrive as price. It arrives as sequence: the input that comes late, the approval
        that does not come, the person who cannot be hired in time.</p>
        <p>What that exposes is operational debt. The sequence nobody set, the dependency
        nobody removed, the decision that was never actually taken. It carries no cost
        while conditions hold, and it is called in when they change.</p>
        <p>Resilience is that debt repaid in advance. It cannot be bought at the point of
        failure, which is the only point at which most organisations go looking for it.</p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="wrap sect">
      <p class="sec-mark mono">The work</p>
      <div class="sect-body">
      <h2 class="band-title reveal">One standard, four capabilities.</h2>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>There is no single description of the work. It is commissioned when something
        critical has to be designed, built, put right or made ready, and usually because
        it has not been done before by the people commissioning it. The sector and the
        asset change with every engagement.</p>
        <p>How the work is done does not change. Every engagement runs through the same
        four capabilities, <a href={withBase('/services')}>design, build, integrate and
        communicate</a>, and everything they produce is held to the same standard:
        <a href={withBase('/about')}>resilience, contingency, redundancy and flow</a>.</p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof">
    <div class="wrap sect">
      <p class="coord mono reveal">Standing</p>
      <div class="sect-body">
      <h2 class="reveal">Proven under pressure, <em>not in theory.</em></h2>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>The method did not come from theory. It was formed in high-risk operations,
        where margins are constructed rather than assumed. Precision in the planning,
        craft in the execution, disciplined use of the resource available, and procedures
        that still hold when the conditions change.</p>
        <p>Robust by design, resilient in use.</p>
        <p>The risk is resolved in advance. The plan assumes failure at each critical
        point and carries a second route for it, and what cannot be anticipated is left to
        judgement, held by people trained to exercise it.</p>
        <p>The work changes with every engagement; the pattern does not.</p>
        <p>The standard: resilience, contingency, redundancy and flow, transposes
        because fragility has the same shape wherever it appears. Discipline is what makes
        an operation run predictably and keep running through adversity.</p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="services">
    <div class="wrap sect">
      <p class="sec-mark mono">What we do</p>
      <div class="sect-body">
      <a class="rowlink" href={withBase('/services/design')}><div class="row reveal">
        <div class="body"><h3>Design</h3><p>What should exist, how it works, and in what order. Architecture, structure and sequence, with the decisions that have to be taken before anything is committed.</p></div>
        <span class="go">View →</span>
      </div></a>
      <a class="rowlink" href={withBase('/services/build')}><div class="row reveal">
        <div class="body"><h3>Build</h3><p>Make it. Not a specification handed to someone else, but the working thing: systems, procedures, automation, and people trained to run it.</p></div>
        <span class="go">View →</span>
      </div></a>
      <a class="rowlink" href={withBase('/services/integrate')}><div class="row reveal">
        <div class="body"><h3>Integrate</h3><p>Put it into the organisation so it holds. It runs without us, and it depends on no one person.</p></div>
        <span class="go">View →</span>
      </div></a>
      <a class="rowlink" href={withBase('/services/communicate')}><div class="row reveal">
        <div class="body"><h3>Communicate</h3><p>The record and the telling. Film, sound and the written word, for work that has to be understood by people who were not there.</p></div>
        <span class="go">View →</span>
      </div></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contact" id="contact">
    <div class="wrap sect">
      <p class="sec-mark mono reveal">Contact</p>
      <div class="sect-body">
      <h2 class="reveal">Engagements open with an assessment.</h2>
      <div class="prose reveal" style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-l)">
        <p>We establish what the work actually requires before anything is proposed.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost reveal" href={withBase(cta.href)}>{cta.label}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {clients.length > 0 && (
    <section class="clients">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="sec-mark reveal">Previous clients, collaborators and partners:</p>
        <div class="clientstrip">
          <div class="clientstrip-track">
          <div class="clientstrip-group">
            {clients.map((c) => c.src
              ? <a class="client-logo" href={c.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                   style={`--logo-src:url("${withBase(c.src)}");--logo-ratio:${c.ratio ?? 3};--logo-scale:${c.scale ?? 1}`}>
                  <span class="visually-hidden">{c.name}</span>
                </a>
              : <a class="client-word" href={c.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{c.name}</a>)}
          </div>
            <div class="clientstrip-group" aria-hidden="true">
              {clients.map((c) => c.src
                ? <a class="client-logo" href={c.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" tabindex="-1"
                     style={`--logo-src:url("${withBase(c.src)}");--logo-ratio:${c.ratio ?? 3};--logo-scale:${c.scale ?? 1}`}></a>
                : <a class="client-word" href={c.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" tabindex="-1">{c.name}</a>)}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}
</BaseLayout>
